WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:08.033
In this walkthrough we'll set up a
user record and see where their
access comes from, in the OpenTRMS Workbench.

2
00:00:08.033 --> 00:00:19.467
The User Access Workbook is the administrator's view of
who can use the system. It opens on the directory — every
user, with their login identifier, status and last sign-in.

3
00:00:19.467 --> 00:00:32.800
Four tabs sit above it. Everything you do here applies to
whichever user is selected, so you pick a person once and then
work across profile, memberships, entitlements and review without losing them.

4
00:00:32.800 --> 00:00:45.300
New user pre-provisions a record. It is worth knowing that
this step is optional — if someone signs in and no record
exists, one is created for them automatically on that first request.

5
00:00:45.300 --> 00:00:55.700
The subject is the login identifier, and it has to
match whatever the identity provider will send — a
corporate email address, or a directory user ID like this one.

6
00:00:55.700 --> 00:01:03.600
The display name is what colleagues will see
against approvals and audit entries, so it
should read as a person rather than an account.

7
00:01:03.600 --> 00:01:12.767
Create the user, and the record appears in
the directory straight away. It is active
immediately, but on its own it grants nothing.

8
00:01:12.767 --> 00:01:19.900
Selecting the new user loads them into the tabs
above, and everything from here applies to them.

9
00:01:19.900 --> 00:01:31.500
Memberships is where data groups are granted — these
decide which books, portfolios and counterparties the
person can see, and the table records who added each one and when.

10
00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:45.633
A group is chosen here and added, and what it grants is data access —
which books and counterparties the person can see. Functional groups,
which carry what a person is allowed to do, are listed separately below.

11
00:01:45.633 --> 00:01:57.867
The last two tabs complete the picture. Entitlements shows
what the person can actually do once their groups are applied,
and Access Review is where that access is signed off periodically.

12
00:01:57.867 --> 00:02:05.833
That completes Users and Access. Every surface
shown here can also be opened from the agent
panel on the right, by asking for it in plain English.
